 and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=0, &  & b(t)=2, &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=1, &  & d(t)=-1, &  & g(t)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the terms ${x}_{1}^{2}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}(t).$\n\n- System III is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=7, &  & b(t)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t), &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=-1, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314795 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129314 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66d19e98-522f-5db2-b340-0f35ba2ece23" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "385ba27a-e049-525b-a5d8-dc375ac40522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312431} {:answer/id #uuid "5d706bb9-8917-5f9b-87f5-2f2eb19da810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312721} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff99d3e-e281-5989-a314-caaa6c8573c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312743} {:answer/id #uuid "8b3f91dc-d67f-5295-be0d-c243d8997671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313085} {:answer/id #uuid "d57330ed-602f-5498-83d1-414994e3b76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313657}] 