 below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/90/9003cc9588b0838527f018463e2077d2d81bb5930ab70c1e3c713832e207bd99.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=2$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is false, while statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-2$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314832 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147495 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75ca2003-0bf5-51f7-a56a-6494e61a1a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312913} {:answer/id #uuid "a44e30a6-55cc-547c-89a4-36a7d494b589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313267} {:answer/id #uuid "c413c015-fa40-508d-b83f-c99fd7911d88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313516} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d82aed-e0de-54d4-8293-afeff2b44f92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313913} {:answer/id #uuid "fc72c4d3-bc8a-5f0d-be5d-7ac8569ecce9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218631398